# Frontend Docker Build

## NPM registry (build)

`main.Dockerfile` and `dev.Dockerfile` default `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` to the **same Liara mirror as the backend**:

`https://package-mirror.liara.ir/repository/npm/`

They also define `NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL` as:

`https://mirror-npm.runflare.com/`

And `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL` as:

`https://registry.npmjs.org/`

Every builder-stage `pnpm` step (install **and** `pnpm run build`) runs through `.cursor/docker/fallback-registry.sh` with a Corepack cache mount. The script tries registries in order — Liara, then Runflare, then npmjs.org — and stops at the first one that succeeds.

Without this on the build step, Corepack re-downloads `pnpm@10.28.2` from `registry.npmjs.org` (default) in a new `RUN` layer where the install-time cache mount and registry env vars are gone — which fails on CI networks that only reach the Liara mirror.

Override at build time when needed:

```bash
docker build \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_URL="https://…" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL="https://mirror-npm.runflare.com/" \
  --build-arg NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL="https://registry.npmjs.org/" \
  -f apps/frontend/main.Dockerfile .
```

`COREPACK_NPM_REGISTRY`, `npm_config_registry`, and `pnpm config set registry` all use this URL so Corepack can fetch `pnpm@10.28.2` and `pnpm install` uses the same mirror.

## CI defaults

- **GitLab** (`build:frontend` in `.gitlab-ci.yml`): passes `NPM_REGISTRY_URL`, `NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL`, and `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL`
- **GitHub Actions** (`frontend-cicd.yml`): passes the same build args from secrets or repo defaults

Set the `NPM_REGISTRY_URL` CI variable to override the primary registry for all pipelines. Override `NPM_REGISTRY_SECOND_FALLBACK_URL` or `NPM_REGISTRY_FALLBACK_URL` when needed.

## Docker Hub / base images

Base images use the Arvan Docker mirror prefix (`docker.arvancloud.ir/node:22-alpine`). See [docker-hub-mirror-arvan.mdc](docker-hub-mirror-arvan.mdc).

## Node version

Frontend Dockerfiles use **Node 22** (`node:22-alpine`) for Next.js cache handler / Web Streams compatibility under load. Backend uses Node 20 for Strapi 4.x engine compatibility.
